---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Weigh Easy - Support"
  description="Get help with Weigh Easy - Private Weight Tracker iOS app."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/weigh-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Weigh Easy?</p>
          <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Weigh%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I add a weigh-in?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Type your weight in the field at the bottom of Today, like 182.4, and tap Add. You can add a unit, a day and a note in the same line: “82.5 kg yesterday after a run”. Weigh Easy shows what it understood before it saves. For every detail, tap the edit button at the top right of Today.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What does the trend mean?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">The trend line smooths out day-to-day swings from water and food. Several weigh-ins on one day count as their average, and days you skip are skipped rather than guessed, so a break of a few weeks doesn’t pull the line. Today says the trend in words, like “Down 1.2 lb a week”, measured over your last four weeks of weigh-ins.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Why does my weight go up and down so much?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Day-to-day changes of a pound or two are normal: water, meals, exercise and sleep all move the scale. The trend line is there so you can watch the direction rather than each day.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">When is the best time to weigh myself?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">The same time each day gives the most consistent numbers, for many people first thing in the morning. Consistency matters more than the time you pick.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I set a goal?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Tap Set a goal on Today, or open the menu, then Settings, then Goal. Your goal starts from your latest weigh-in; Today shows how much is left, a bar for how far you’ve come, and roughly when you’d get there at your current pace.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I use pounds, kilograms or stones?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. Open Settings and pick Pounds, Kilograms or Stones. Weigh Easy keeps every weight exactly, so switching units never changes your history, and it remembers your choice.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does Weigh Easy work with Apple Health?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes, if you turn it on: open Settings and switch on Apple Health, then tap Continue. Weigh-ins you add in Weigh Easy are saved to Apple Health as Weight, and weights from your smart scale or other apps show up in your trend. Weigh Easy reads and saves only your weight, and nothing from Health leaves your iPhone. To change access later, open the Settings app, then Health, then Data Access &amp; Devices, then Weigh Easy.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Where are my progress photos kept?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Inside Weigh Easy, on your iPhone only. They aren’t added to your photo library or iCloud, and they’re left out of your iPhone backups unless you turn on Settings, then Progress photos, then Include in backups. You can also lock them with Face ID. If you saved photos with an earlier version, which kept them in your photo library, Weigh Easy copies them in and leaves the originals where they are.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I change or delete a weigh-in?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Tap it on Today or in History to change the weight, time or note, or to delete it. In History you can also touch and hold a weigh-in. If Apple Health is on, the change is made there too.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Is my data backed up?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Your weigh-ins, goal and measurements are in your regular iPhone backups (iCloud or computer). Progress photos are left out of backups unless you turn on Include in backups, so by default they stay on this iPhone only and don’t move to a new one. Weigh Easy has no cloud of its own.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I export my data?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. Open Settings, then Data, then Export as CSV, for every weigh-in and measurement in a spreadsheet-friendly file.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does Weigh Easy work on Apple Watch?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. The watch app shows your latest weight, trend and goal, and adds a weigh-in with the Digital Crown. It’s sent to Weigh Easy on your iPhone.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>

<style>
  .faq-item {
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color, #e5e7eb);
  }

  :global(.dark) .faq-item {
    border-bottom-color: #374151;
  }

  .faq-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
